# ---- Server & Mode ----
PORT=4000
NODE_ENV=development
# DRY_RUN=true => paper trading only, zero capital, no on-chain transaction is ever signed.
DRY_RUN=true
TZ=Asia/Jakarta

# ---- AI Provider (DeepSeek, OpenAI-compatible) ----
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=your_deepseek_api_key_here
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
DEEPSEEK_MODEL_CHAT=deepseek-chat
DEEPSEEK_MODEL_REASONER=deepseek-reasoner

# ---- Solana & Meteora ----
SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=your_helius_key
METEORA_API_URL=https://dlmm.datapi.meteora.ag
# Only used when DRY_RUN=false (live mode is not implemented yet). Leave blank.
# Read from the environment ONLY. Never paste a key into source; src/tests/liveConfig.test.ts
# fails the build if a base58 secret ever appears under src/.
SOLANA_PRIVATE_KEY=
# The wallet's PUBLIC address. Used only to read a balance for the startup gas check and
# for the dashboard's portfolio hero (GET /api/wallet), and deliberately separate from the
# key above so the probe never touches secret material. Unset = the hero reports
# "not configured" rather than a fabricated $0.00.
SOLANA_WALLET_ADDRESS=
# Display name on the portfolio hero. Configured, never derived: an address is not a name.
WALLET_LABEL=Main Wallet

# ---- Paper baseline ----
# The number every reported percentage is measured against (netPnlPct, drawdown,
# currentBalanceUSD). Unset = $1000, which is backed by nothing.
#
# PIN IT HERE once you know your figure. This is the only reproducible option: an
# explicit baseline survives a restart, so the same trade history always reports the
# same percentages.
#
# STARTING_BALANCE_USD=116.08
#
# Alternatively STARTING_BALANCE_FROM_WALLET-style seeding happens automatically at
# preflight when the live profile is armed AND the database holds no closed trades: the
# baseline is taken from the real wallet (SOL x price) and the boot log prints the exact
# line to paste above. It refuses to rebase a database that already has trades, because
# every percentage already reported against the old baseline would silently change
# meaning. Note a wallet-derived baseline is RE-DERIVED each boot and drifts with the
# wallet — pin it as soon as you have the number.

# ---- Telegram Dispatcher ----
# Leave both blank to silently disable Telegram notifications.
# Telegram: bot token + chat for alerts; ALLOWED_USER_IDS = comma-separated
# Telegram user IDs allowed to run control commands (/status, /close_all,
# /pause, /resume). Empty = everyone is denied (fail closed).
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USER_IDS=

# ---- Paper Trading Engine ----
VIRTUAL_SOL_PER_POSITION=1.0
MAX_CONCURRENT_POSITIONS=3
TAKE_PROFIT_PCT=5.0
STOP_LOSS_PCT=-8.0
MAX_POSITION_AGE_HOURS=24

# ---- Screener Thresholds ----
MIN_24H_VOLUME_USD=10000
MIN_FEE_TVL_RATIO=0.008
MIN_TVL_USD=50000
# Outlier guard: reject pools reporting an implausible 24h fee/TVL ratio
# (0.25 = 25%/24h). Set to 999 to disable.
MAX_FEE_TVL_RATIO=0.25

# ---- Anti-Rug Screen ----
ANTIRUG_ENABLED=true
ANTIRUG_MAX_TOP10_HOLDER_PCT=25
ANTIRUG_REQUIRE_MINT_REVOKED=true
ANTIRUG_REQUIRE_FREEZE_REVOKED=true
# What an unverifiable check means: reject (fail closed, default) | allow (fail open).
# NOTE: the public Solana RPC blocks getTokenLargestAccounts (HTTP 429), so with the
# default endpoint every candidate resolves to UNKNOWN and is rejected. Use a paid RPC
# (Helius/Triton/QuickNode) or set this to "allow" to trade unscreened pools.
ANTIRUG_ON_ERROR=reject

# ---- Failure-Avoidance Guardrails (validated out-of-sample) ----
# Four hard gates. Together they cut the rate of losses worse than -10% from 6.5%
# to 1.5% in-sample and 8.3% to 0.9% out-of-sample on ~13k enumerated entries.
# These are EXCLUSIONS, not a score: the composite score did not replicate, so
# ranking is left to the plain fee/TVL x volume rule.
MIN_POOL_AGE_HOURS=48
MAX_PRICE_SURGE_1H_PCT=10
MAX_REALIZED_VOL_PCT_PER_HOUR=20
MAX_TVL_USD=500000

# ---- Priority Fee Estimation ----
PRIORITY_FEE_PERCENTILE=75
PRIORITY_FEE_COMPUTE_UNITS=200000

# ---- Post-Trade Reflection ----
POST_MORTEM_ENABLED=true

# ---- Friction / gas optimisation ----
# Floor on the bin range the LLM may choose. A tight range exits sooner and every exit
# burns gas + forced-exit slippage; the unbiased backtest showed friction ($74.80)
# exceeding all fee income ($55.25), so the range is widened by default.
MIN_DOWNSIDE_COVER_PCT=45
MIN_UPSIDE_COVER_PCT=15
FORCED_EXIT_SLIPPAGE_PCT=2.0
# A pool must earn at least this multiple of its round-trip cost in 24h of fees, or
# the entry is skipped.
MIN_FEE_COST_COVERAGE=2.5
# Volatility gate: reject tokens that pumped more than this in 24h.
# Unknown 24h change is rejected too (reject | allow).
MAX_PRICE_CHANGE_24H_PCT=150
VOLATILITY_ON_UNKNOWN=reject

# ---- Engine version cohorts (dashboard Session/Cohort filter) ----
# The instant the v1.1 "clean engine" took over: anti-churn gates + the 60s exit monitor.
# Positions OPENED at or after this are v1.1; earlier ones are v1.0 legacy. Opened, not
# closed -- the cohort names the engine that made the ENTRY decision.
#
# Default is the v1.1 commit. NOT midnight 2026-08-29: 13 of the 27 legacy trades were
# opened later that same morning (last at 12:40Z), so a date-only cutoff would file
# pre-fix trades under "Clean Engine".
#
# SET THIS TO YOUR ACTUAL v1.1 RESTART TIME. The commit time is a safe floor, not a
# deploy record -- trades opened between the commit and the restart are still v1.0's.
ENGINE_V11_CUTOFF=2026-08-29T13:20:40Z

# Longest gap a single monitor tick may accrue fees for. Fees are rate x (now -
# last_checked_at), so after downtime that span is however long the engine was off: a 52h
# restart gap once credited two days of fees in one tick, on one instantaneous in-range
# check of a period nothing was watching. Generous next to the 60s monitor, so normal
# operation never reaches it.
MAX_FEE_ACCRUAL_GAP_HOURS=1

# ---- Fast position monitor ----
# Marks open positions every 60s, decoupled from the 10-minute screener. A -8% stop-loss
# is only as tight as the interval that tests it: on the 10-minute cadence the dry run
# closed one at -13.84%. Set false to fall back to monitoring at screener cadence.
FAST_MONITOR_ENABLED=true

# ---- In-context learning for the entry model ----
# How many recent losing closes are quoted back to DeepSeek when it picks a pool. Only
# closes that already carry a post-mortem count. 0 disables the block.
LOSS_CONTEXT_TRADES=5

# ---- Anti-churn: pool cooldown & failure lockout ----
# The screener has no memory of its own trades, so a pool that keeps ranking first keeps
# getting re-entered minutes after it was closed out of range — paying gas and forced-exit
# slippage every lap. These two gates give it that memory. Both run before the anti-rug
# screen; set either to 0 to disable it.
#
# Cooldown: exclude a pool for this many hours after ANY of its positions closes.
POOL_COOLDOWN_HOURS=4
# Lockout: consecutive CLOSED_LOSS / CLOSED_OUT_OF_RANGE closes that trip the breaker.
# The run is counted newest-first and reset by any other outcome (a win, a timeout).
POOL_LOCKOUT_CONSECUTIVE_FAILURES=2
# How long a tripped pool stays locked out, measured from its last failure.
POOL_LOCKOUT_HOURS=24

# ---- Optional: TradFi macro via FRED (free key) ----
# https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
FRED_API_KEY=

# ---- Optional: deep backtest history via CoinGecko Pro ----
# GeckoTerminal's keyless tier serves roughly 208 days of hourly OHLCV and answers
# HTTP 401 on any deeper page; daily aggregation is capped at the same depth, so a
# coarser timeframe buys no history. `npm run backtest:annual` therefore simulates a
# ~6-month window unless this key is set, and says so in its header and caveats.
# https://www.coingecko.com/en/api/pricing
COINGECKO_PRO_API_KEY=

# ---- Database ----
DATABASE_PATH=./data/flowmetrix.db

# ---- Live micro-capital profile ----
# Values below are the DEPLOYED live profile (7 Sep 2026, wallet ~3.10 SOL).
# Code defaults in src/config/liveConfig.ts stay at the 1.15 SOL envelope; the live
# server overrides them via .env (untracked). Mirror these if you deploy the same
# wallet size. Raising LIVE_CAPITAL_SOL is the sanctioned coverage lever: it buys
# rent headroom, and rent is recovered when the position closes.
#
# It does not touch the V1.1 baseline. Cooldown (4h), lockout (2 -> 24h),
# MIN_FEE_COST_COVERAGE (2.5x), the 30m/60s clocks and the 16k reasoning cap are
# unchanged; the dollar floor below is stacked ON TOP of the 2.5x ratio gate.
LIVE_MICRO_CAPITAL=true

# Capital & sizing. Positions are sized from FREE capital: capital - reserve - open
# notional. The profile is rejected at boot if maxPosition x concurrent could ever
# reach the reserve (3.05: 1.8 x 1 = 1.8 of 2.90 deployable, 1.10 SOL of rent slack).
#
# 1.10 SOL of rent headroom admits any pool up to the 1400-bin program limit
# (~0.996 SOL account rent) = 93.2% coverage; the original 1.15 SOL envelope left
# 0.20 SOL = 278 bins = 74.3%. One concentrated position rather than several small
# ones: gas is per transaction and does not shrink with the position.
LIVE_CAPITAL_SOL=3.05
LIVE_MAX_POSITION_SOL=1.8
LIVE_MAX_CONCURRENT_POSITIONS=1
# Untouchable, for gas and rent-exempt minimums. A position that cannot pay for its own
# close makes the stop-loss unenforceable.
LIVE_MIN_RESERVE_SOL=0.15

# Friction. The gas figure is a FLOOR, not just a fallback: the live p75 estimate is
# used only when it is HIGHER. An unavailable estimate is never priced at zero.
LIVE_ROUND_TRIP_GAS_SOL=0.008
# Minimum projected net PnL (fees over the horizon, minus gas and forced-exit slippage).
# At 1.8 SOL (~$200) this floor demands ~0.75% fee/TVL in 24h. Note it is NOT the binding
# constraint at this size: the V1.1 2.5x coverage gate independently demands ~9% on the
# micro profile, and a pool must clear both. Which gate binds flips with position size,
# so the engine prints BOTH plus the binding one at boot; read that before assuming an
# empty candidate list is a bug. (At the previous 0.20 SOL the bar was 15%.)
LIVE_MIN_NET_PNL_USD=1.50
LIVE_PNL_HORIZON_HOURS=24

# Startup gas gate. A wallet below this refuses to start the engine and sends a Telegram
# INSUFFICIENT_GAS_RESERVE alert. A balance that cannot be READ is treated the same way:
# an unverified wallet is not a funded one.
LIVE_MIN_WALLET_SOL=0.20

# ---- On-chain execution (LIVE — wired into the engine since 6 Sep 2026) ----
# src/services/onchainExecutor.ts signs and submits Solana transactions; liveExecution
# calls it for every entry/exit when DRY_RUN=false. Keep this false for paper only.
ONCHAIN_EXECUTION_ARMED=true

# Blast radius of a bug in live code: ceiling per transaction, in lamports.
# Must be >= the max position deposit or the boot validator refuses to start
# ("every entry would pass screening and then fail the spend ceiling"). Rent is
# charged to this ceiling on BOTH the narrow (atomic) and wide (create + chunked
# liquidity) paths. Deployed value matches LIVE_MAX_POSITION_SOL=1.8:
ONCHAIN_MAX_LAMPORTS_PER_TX=1800000000

# Slippage bound in basis points. 50 = 0.5%. This may only be LOWERED: the hard cap is
# a constant in the module and configuration cannot widen it.
ONCHAIN_MAX_SLIPPAGE_BPS=50

# Operator pool denylist (comma-separated pool addresses and/or pair names,
# case-insensitive). Checked in openLivePosition BEFORE any network call or swap —
# a denied pool is a routine seekNewEntry skip, never a spend. Added 7 Sep 2026
# after STONK-SOL (zxTpi4BtaWX3mgdAPoezkMD1hxx8CdeCfrqXMWvSCLX) cost real money
# twice in one day; this is the escape hatch for "that pool specifically, gone".
# STONK-SOL is filled in here as the worked example, NOT as a claim about what the
# live host runs - this repository cannot see that host's .env and must not pretend
# to. It is written out rather than left blank because a blank example is what gets
# copied when re-provisioning, and copying it would re-arm the pool that cost
# 0.4 SOL and then 0.27 SOL in one day. Confirm what is ACTUALLY armed by reading
# the boot line: `[guard] execution breaker: ...; operator denylist: ...`.
POOL_DENYLIST=zxTpi4BtaWX3mgdAPoezkMD1hxx8CdeCfrqXMWvSCLX

# AUTOMATIC counterpart to the denylist above, and the one that matters more, because it
# needs nobody to be awake. Counts consecutive on-chain EXECUTION failures per pool and
# benches the pool when it hits the limit.
#
# Deliberately NOT the same thing as POOL_LOCKOUT_CONSECUTIVE_FAILURES, which counts
# failed EXITS reconstructed from closed position rows. A failed OPEN writes no row - by
# design - so the V1.1 lockout is structurally blind to it, which is why the same pool
# was re-elected every 30 minutes on 7 Sep 2026. Set either to 0 to disable.
EXECUTION_FAILURE_LOCKOUT_COUNT=2
EXECUTION_FAILURE_LOCKOUT_HOURS=24

# Dynamic priority fee. Most slots report a zero prioritization fee, so a sampled p75 is
# often 0, and a zero-fee transaction is exactly the one that hangs when Solana is busy.
# The floor prevents that; the ceiling bounds what escalation may cost. The fee escalates
# only when a transaction is REBUILT after its blockhash expired, never per rebroadcast.
#
# ONCHAIN_COMPUTE_UNIT_LIMIT is a FLOOR, not a cap. Where the DLMM SDK sizes a
# transaction higher than this - it simulates most of its calls against the cluster, and
# budgets 1,000,000 CU for chunked add-liquidity and 350,000 per bin-array init - the
# SDK's larger figure is what gets installed, clamped to Solana's 1,400,000 ceiling.
# Until 7 Sep 2026 this value OVERRODE the SDK's, and every operation sized above it
# died on the compute meter after the balancing swap had already spent. Raising it costs
# priority fee (price x REQUESTED units); lowering it below ~400k buys nothing, because
# the SDK's own estimate is what binds on the transactions that matter.
ONCHAIN_COMPUTE_UNIT_LIMIT=400000
ONCHAIN_MIN_PRIORITY_MICRO_LAMPORTS=20000
ONCHAIN_MAX_PRIORITY_MICRO_LAMPORTS=2000000
ONCHAIN_PRIORITY_ESCALATION=2.0
ONCHAIN_MAX_BUILD_ATTEMPTS=3

# Jupiter keyless swap API. quote-api.jup.ag/v6 is dead (DNS); this host is the live one
# and matches the price endpoint the engine already uses.
JUPITER_SWAP_API_URL=https://lite-api.jup.ag/swap/v1
